>> title: Adobo para Al Pastor
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: mexican, chiles, achiote, pineapple, marinade, pork
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: adobada marinade, al pastor marinade, adobo para tacos al pastor, marinada de achiote, adobo rojo, pastor marinade
>> pairs-with: al-pastor
>> servings: 8
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — thirty seconds a side is the whole toast, and a guajillo taken past that is bitter through every slice of pork it later coats with nothing to correct it; the twenty-minute soak and the five-minute simmer after it ask nothing of you
>> step.1: toast 30 sec a side, soak 20 min
>> step.2: blend smooth
>> step.3: strain
>> step.4: simmer 5 min, cool

Toast @dried guajillo chiles{6}(stemmed and seeded) and @dried ancho chiles{2}(stemmed and seeded) in a dry #comal{} for ~toast{30%sec} a side, until they smell of raisins, then press them under @hot water{1 1/2%cup}(360 mL) to soak for ~soak{20%min}.

Blend @&(~1)soaked chiles{} with @achiote paste{2%Tbs}(recado rojo), @pineapple juice{3/4%cup}(180 mL), @white vinegar{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @garlic{5%cloves}, @white onion{1/2%medium}(chopped), @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @ground cloves{1/4%tsp}, @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, and @sugar{1%tsp} until completely smooth.

Strain @&(~1)adobo{} through a #fine-mesh sieve{}, working it through with a ladle and leaving the chile skins behind.

Simmer @&(~1)strained adobo{} with @lard{1%Tbs} in a #saucepan{} over medium heat for ~simmer{5%min}, until it darkens and coats the spoon, then cool it before it meets the pork.
